    description: "**Defect.** The reproducibility guarantee text references a field that is absent from the captured block and null on the dominant pass.\n\n**Evidence.** `reproducibility_context.implications` says maps with matching `pass_versions` (among other fields) should be functionally identical. But the captured keys are {grammars, hypergumbo_version, python_implementation, python_version, tree_sitter_version} — `pass_versions` is NOT among them, so a consumer cannot find it in the block the text describes; the per-pass version must be dug out of analysis_runs, where it is empty for 14 of 84 runs — including the dominant Python pass (~852 files).\n\n**Contract.** The reproducibility contract should reference fields that are actually captured in the reproducibility block and populated for the passes that matter.\n\n**Consequence.** The documented reproducibility guarantee rests on a field a consumer cannot use as written; reproducibility comparison is unreliable for the dominant pass.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** WI-mifok (wont_do) covers pass_version being empty on 14/84 runs; INV-pitab the broader provenance-field-set defect. This is the distinct surface: the implications text references pass_versions absent from `reproducibility_context.captured`."  # 6748
